{
  "preset": "Lab: break a weak key over the air (no radio)",
  "description": "The whole story on one canvas, no radio needed. Top chain: a message is modulated (AFSK 1200), sent through a noisy channel and demodulated - the text comes out READABLE. Bottom chain: the same message is XOR-encrypted with a 1-byte key first, so after the identical demodulation it is SCRAMBLED. The Brute force block then tries all 256 one-byte keys, recognises the readable result and recovers the message - so a 1-byte key protects nothing. It also prints how long the same search would take for a real 128-bit key (far longer than the age of the universe).",
